The system transition operator $\mathbf{T}_{ij}$ between layer $L_i$ and layer $L_j$ enforces the necessary condition:

$$\forall (L_i, L_j) \in \mathcal{E}, \quad \text{ker}(\mathbf{T}_{ij}) = \{\mathbf{0}\} \implies \left( \Delta S(L_i) \neq 0 \implies \Delta S(L_j) = \mathbf{T}_{ij} \Delta S(L_i) \right)$$

No downstream state transition $\Delta S(L_j)$ can execute without strict pre-state validity at all antecedent nodes $\text{Anc}(L_j) \subseteq \mathcal{V}$.

