### 2. Deterministic Financial Invariants & State Equations

#### 2.1. Net Debit Settlement Invariant (DTC / NSCC)

For any participant $k \in \mathcal{P}$ at intraday time $t$, the accumulated net debit position $D_k(t)$ is bounded by the Net Debit Cap $\mathcal{C}_k$ and the Collateral Monitor $\mathcal{M}_k(t)$:

$$D_k(t) = \sum_{m=1}^{M} \text{GrossDebit}_{k,m}(t) - \sum_{n=1}^{N} \text{GrossCredit}_{k,n}(t)$$

$$\text{Invariant 1 (Cap Bound):} \quad D_k(t) \le \mathcal{C}_k \le \min\left( \text{QLR}_{\text{DTC}}, \; \text{CapLimit}_{\text{Regulatory}} \right)$$

$$\text{Invariant 2 (Collateral Sufficiency):} \quad \mathcal{M}_k(t) = V_{\text{collateral}}(k, t) \cdot (1 - h_{\text{haircut}}) - D_k(t) \ge 0$$

where $\text{QLR}_{\text{DTC}} = \$1.15\text{B (Participants Fund)} + \$1.90\text{B (Committed Credit Line)} + \text{Cash proceeds from Senior Notes}$.

#### 2.2. Multilateral Netting Compression Ratio

The trade novation operator $\mathcal{N}: \mathbb{R}^{E_{\text{gross}}} \to \mathbb{R}^{E_{\text{net}}}$ compresses market gross obligations to single net deliver/receive quantities:

$$\gamma_{\text{netting}} = 1 - \frac{\sum_{k \in \mathcal{P}} \left( \left\vert{} \sum_{i} Q_{i,k}^{\text{buy}} - \sum_{j} Q_{j,k}^{\text{sell}} \right\vert{} \cdot P_{\text{settle}} \right)}{\sum_{k \in \mathcal{P}} \sum_{m} \left( Q_{m,k}^{\text{gross}} \cdot P_{m} \right)}$$

Under equity Continuous Net Settlement (CNS), $\gamma_{\text{netting}} \ge 0.98$ (98%+ settlement liquidity compression).

#### 2.3. Margin Requirement & Supplemental Liquidity (SLD) Formula

The total clearing margin for participant $k$ under SEC Rule 17ad-22(e)(6) is:

$$\text{Margin}_k = \max\left( \text{VaR}_{99\%}^{10\text{Y}}(k) + \text{StressPeriodAddon}(k), \; \text{VaR Floor}(k) \right) + \text{ECP}_k + \text{SLD}_k$$

where the Excess Capital Premium ($\text{ECP}_k$) activates when:

$$\text{Calculated Margin}_k > \alpha \cdot \text{Excess Net Capital}_k \implies \text{ECP}_k = \left( \frac{\text{Calculated Margin}_k - \alpha \cdot \text{Net Capital}_k}{\text{Net Capital}_k} \right) \cdot \text{Calculated Margin}_k$$

and $\text{SLD}_k$ enforces liquidity coverage during peak volume stress:

$$\text{SLD}_k(t) = \max\left(0, \; \text{PeakNetObligation}_k(t) - \text{Prefunded QLR}_{\text{NSCC}}\right)$$

