### 3. Loss Allocation Waterfall: Piecewise Depletion Operator

Upon participant default $\mathcal{D}_{\text{member}}$ at time $t_0$, the loss absorption function $\mathcal{W}(L_{\text{loss}})$ executes along a deterministic sequence:

$$\mathcal{W}(L_{\text{loss}}) = \sum_{s=1}^{6} \Delta R_s$$

$$\Delta R_1 = \min\left( L_{\text{loss}}, \; \text{ClearingFund}(\mathcal{D}) + \text{CollateralPledged}(\mathcal{D}) \right)$$

$$\Delta R_2 = \min\left( \max(0, L_{\text{loss}} - R_1), \; \text{CrossGuarantyAllocation}(\text{DTC}, \text{NSCC}, \text{FICC}, \text{OCC}) \right)$$

$$\Delta R_3 = \min\left( \max(0, L_{\text{loss}} - R_1 - R_2), \; 0.50 \times \text{CapitalRequirement}_{\text{GBR}} \right)$$

$$\Delta R_4 = \min\left( \max(0, L_{\text{loss}} - \sum_{i=1}^3 R_i), \; \sum_{k \neq \mathcal{D}} \text{ClearingFund}_k \cdot \frac{\text{ReqDeposit}_k}{\sum \text{ReqDeposit}} \right)$$

$$\Delta R_5 = \min\left( \max(0, L_{\text{loss}} - \sum_{i=1}^4 R_i), \; \text{CappedAssessmentCalls}(\mathcal{P}_{\text{solvent}}) \right)$$

$$\Delta R_6 = \text{PRO (Variation Margin Haircutting)} \; \longrightarrow \; \text{Partial/Full Tear-Ups} \; \longrightarrow \; \text{Recovery \& Wind-Down (R\&W)}$$

